  "term": "personal unconscious",
  "definition": "In Jungian theory, the personal unconscious is the part of the unconscious made up of a person’s own repressed or forgotten experiences, thoughts, and feelings. It is distinguished from the collective unconscious, which is described as inherited and universal.",
